.TH SDL_HINT_RENDER_DRIVER 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_RENDER_DRIVER \- A variable specifying which render driver to use.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_RENDER_DRIVER \(dqSDL_RENDER_DRIVER\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If the application doesn\(aqt pick a specific renderer to use, this variable specifies the name of the preferred renderer\[char46] If the preferred renderer can\(aqt be initialized, creating a renderer will fail\[char46]
.PP
This variable is case insensitive and can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dqdirect3d\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqdirect3d11\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqdirect3d12\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqopengl\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqopengles2\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqopengles\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqmetal\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqvulkan\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqgpu\(dq
.PP
\(bu \(dqsoftware\(dq
.PP
This hint accepts a comma-separated list of driver names, and each will be tried in the order listed when creating a renderer until one succeeds or all of them fail\[char46]
.PP
The default varies by platform, but it\(aqs the first one in the list that is available on the current platform\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before creating a renderer\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

